    "result": "I implemented `RateLimiter` in `solution.py` to the spec, and the 17 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\nIt keeps each client's accepted requests as (time, cost) pairs. A request counts only while `now - t < window_seconds`, so a request exactly one window old has expired. `retry_after` works out how many units must free up, then walks the oldest requests until enough have expired. A call that raises `ValueError` leaves the limiter's latest-time state unchanged.\n\nThe tests cover constructor and cost validation, expiry at the exact window boundary, client independence, rejected requests not using budget, `retry_after` values, queries not recording anything, and time going backwards across clients.",
